<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SAMUEL YELLEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Samuel Yellen is a renowned American novelist honored with both the Guggenheim Fellowship and the EMET Prize, known for his nuanced exploration of the human experience and unique storytelling abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUGGENHEIM FELLOWSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Guggenheim Fellowship is a prestigious grant recognizing excellence in the arts, established in 1925, and has honored notable figures such as Ernest Hemingway, Langston Hughes, and Toni Morrison."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN SIMON GUGGENHEIM MEMORIAL FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The John Simon Guggenheim Memorial Foundation is responsible for awarding the Guggenheim Fellowship, providing financial support and creative freedom to its recipients."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMET PRIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The EMET Prize is an annual award recognizing excellence in art, science, and culture, presented at the prestigious Habima Theater in Tel Aviv, Israel."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HABIMA THEATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Habima Theater is a renowned venue in Tel Aviv, Israel, hosting the annual EMET Prize ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEL AVIV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tel Aviv is a bustling city in Israel, known for its vibrant cultural scene and the annual EMET Prize ceremony held there."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERNEST HEMINGWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ernest Hemingway is a literary giant and a past recipient of the Guggenheim Fellowship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LANGSTON HUGHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Langston Hughes is a literary giant and a past recipient of the Guggenheim Fellowship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TONI MORRISON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toni Morrison is a literary giant and a past recipient of the Guggenheim Fellowship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICHAEL CUNNINGHAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Michael Cunningham is a Pulitzer Prize-winning author who praises Samuel Yellen's talent and impact on American literature."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. EDWARD HIRSCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Edward Hirsch is the President of the John Simon Guggenheim Memorial Foundation, who acknowledges Samuel Yellen's talent and dedication to his craft."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PULITZER PRIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Pulitzer Prize is a prestigious award in the field of journalism, literature, and music, and Michael Cunningham is a past recipient."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Pulitzer Prize is a prestigious award in the field of journalism, literature, and music, mentioned as an honor achieved by Michael Cunningham, a peer of Samuel Yellen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISRAEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Israel is a country known for its rich cultural heritage and the annual EMET Prize ceremony held there."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN LITERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Literature refers to the body of written works produced in the United States, with Samuel Yellen contributing significantly to this field."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LITERARY EXCELLENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Literary Excellence encompasses the quality and skill demonstrated in Samuel Yellen's writing, recognized by both the Guggenheim Fellowship and the EMET Prize."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMIC AND ARTISTIC ELITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Academic and Artistic Elite refers to the distinguished group of scholars and artists who gather at the EMET Prize ceremony, representing the crème de la crème of Israel's intellectual community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CULTURAL HERITAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cultural Heritage refers to the rich cultural traditions and stories that have influenced Samuel Yellen's work, particularly highlighted in his acceptance speech at the EMET Prize ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANCIENT STORIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient Stories are part of Israel's cultural heritage that have inspired Samuel Yellen's work, mentioned in his acceptance speech at the EMET Prize ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESILIENCE OF THE ISRAELI PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Resilience of the Israeli People is a theme that Samuel Yellen explores in his work, mentioned in his acceptance speech at the EMET Prize ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENSE OF COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sense of Community refers to the welcoming environment that Samuel Yellen experienced in Israel, mentioned in his acceptance speech at the EMET Prize ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRITICAL ACCLAIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Critical Acclaim is the recognition and praise that Samuel Yellen's work has received from literary critics and readers, mentioned throughout the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYRICAL PROSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lyrical Prose is a style of writing characterized by its musical quality and emotional depth, mentioned as a hallmark of Samuel Yellen's work."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLEX CHARACTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Complex Characters are a feature of Samuel Yellen's novels, mentioned as a key aspect of his storytelling ability."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOUGHT-PROVOKING THEMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thought-Provoking Themes are the themes explored in Samuel Yellen's work, such as the human experience and the American experience, mentioned throughout the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTALLINE SCULPTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Crystalline Sculpture is the award presented to Samuel Yellen at the EMET Prize ceremony, described as shimmering in the light."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTINGUISHED FELLOWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distinguished Fellows refers to the select group of recipients of the Guggenheim Fellowship, including Samuel Yellen, mentioned in the context of the fellowship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LITERARY GIANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Literary Giants are past recipients of the Guggenheim Fellowship, such as Ernest Hemingway, Langston Hughes, and Toni Morrison, mentioned as examples of distinguished fellows."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREATIVE FREEDOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Creative Freedom is the support provided by the Guggenheim Fellowship, allowing recipients like Samuel Yellen to pursue their next literary project without financial constraints."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINANCIAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial Support is another benefit provided by the Guggenheim Fellowship, enabling recipients like Samuel Yellen to focus on their work without financial worries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOVEL WRITING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Novel Writing is the primary activity of Samuel Yellen, mentioned as his commitment and passion."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST CONTACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First Contact is a metaphorical reference to Samuel Yellen's work capturing the essence of the American experience, mentioned in the context of his novels."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN EXPERIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Human Experience is a recurring theme in Samuel Yellen's work, mentioned as a key aspect of his storytelling."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN EXPERIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Experience is a specific theme in Samuel Yellen's work, mentioned as a key aspect of his storytelling."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLECTIVE ACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collective Action is the impact of Samuel Yellen's work on the literary community, mentioned as a lasting impact on American literature."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUSHING BOUNDARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pushing Boundaries is the innovative approach to literary excellence that Samuel Yellen employs, mentioned as a key aspect of his work."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIS WORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"His work refers to a collective effort or project that has been honored, suggesting a significant organization or institution."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Art represents a form of expression and cultural significance, often involving individuals and communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Culture encompasses the shared beliefs, values, and practices of a community, highlighting the collective aspect of artistic expression."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIVIDUAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Individual refers to a person who contributes to the creation of art and culture, emphasizing personal involvement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLECTIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collective refers to a group of people working together, highlighting the communal aspect of artistic and cultural endeavors."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0415</data>
    </node>
